# The annotations of rex2: the source of src/rex2/*.asm (../../kit/mkgame.py --part src/rex2/rex2.json). Format:
# ../../../../docs/ann-format.md.
@alias ShadowOffset $E4FF-$5800 ; the distance from a screen attribute to its cell in the attribute shadow $E4FF (PowerBar adds it); not an address in the sprites
@isub $B9F5 LD DE,ShadowOffset
@isub $BAA1 LD DE,ShadowOffset

@module graphics ; The development link, the graphics and the level data: the font, the characters, the blocks, the room maps and the sprites
@about The tape loads part 2's code block at $61A8, 400 bytes above part 1's. Its first bytes are the authors' development link, here complete and never overwritten: DevLink $61A8 talks to a host over ports $1F, $3F, $5F, $7F and $7FFD (commands $B4-$BA: poke a block, send a block, page $7FFD, set a breakpoint, return), with the machine's state saved at $62F8. No instruction of the game reaches it. Then come the same tables as part 1, 550 bytes higher ($226): the font (Font $6306, characters 32-95, found at $6206 + 8 x code), the cell type, picture and attribute of the 256 room characters (CharFlags $6506, CharGraphics $6606, CharAttrs $6E06), the 256 blocks of 3 x 3 characters (BlockDefs $6F06), the room maps (RoomMaps $7806, 70 bytes a room; rooms 0-25 are used, RoomExits $B1A7) and the sprites ($8198-$946F).
@about The sprites are stored pre-shifted as in part 1 (a frame list of 8 offsets picks the copy for X & 7; DrawSprite $B296 ORs it into the back buffer). Part 2's enemies are new: kinds 1-5 and 9 have their own pictures and behaviours (ObjectBehaviour $BD27); their names are not in the game (part 2 has no roll call), so the labels name them by kind.
$61A8 b DevLink 16 ; Leftover: the development link's code: pages the link in, saves every register, then serves the host's commands until a return
> OUT to $7F, $3F, $5F, $1F (DevLinkPut) and $7FFD; IN from $3F and $1F; DevLinkGet $62C3 and DevLinkPut $62D3 move one byte with a handshake on port $3F, data on $1F. Commands: $B4 pokes a block (address, length, bytes); $B5 sets the return address ($62BE) and $CD00 ($62BC); $B6 sends a block (address, length; $624E); $B7 pages $7FFD ($6234); $B8 sends the 26 saved bytes at $62E4; $B9 receives 26 bytes there; $BA sets $62BC and $62BE from the host. $B5/$BA end by restoring the registers and calling DebugHook $D6C6. No instruction of the game reaches $61A8 (known only from the code; z80dasm of the bytes); the kit keeps it as bytes because recording c2 reads these bytes once. Kept as a documented leftover (src/res/leftovers/README.md).
@res leftovers/rex2-devlink.bin
$62C3 DevLinkGet ; code: E = a byte from the host (port $1F) after the handshake on port $3F
$62D3 DevLinkPut ; code: a byte to the host (port $1F), then the handshake on port $3F
$62E2 b DevLinkState 8 ; The link's state: a work word, the 26 bytes it sends ($62E4), the saved HL, return address and SP ($62F8, $62FA, $62FC); tape garbage, never written in play
@res leftovers/rex2-devlink.bin
$62FE b Unused62FE 8 ; Eight zero bytes before the font (its codes 24-31 would be here); nothing reads them
@res leftovers/rex2-devlink.bin
$6306 b Font 8 ; The font: 64 characters, codes 32-95 (space to underscore), 8 bytes each, at $6206 + 8 x code
> PrintChar, PrintDigits, the box frame of PrintBoxed ($6346, $6356, $6366, $637E, $63DE, $63EE) and the menu's FontChar $DFB1 read it.
@res fonts/rex2.bin
$6506 b CharFlags 16 ; The cell type of each of the 256 room characters: what Rex and the objects test in the room grid
> DrawRoomCell copies CharFlags[c] into the grid for each character drawn. As in part 1, plus part 2's types: 3 kills Rex when he walks, jumps or falls into it (RexWalkDeadly, RexJumpDeadly, RexFall) and a falling object (ObjectFall $C721), 4 is the big squidgy thing (BossHit $B743), $15 and $16 make walkers dissolve (MaybeDissolve $C5B4, CellDissolve $C5BA).
@res tables/rex2-char-flags.bin
$6606 b CharGraphics 8 ; The 256 room characters, 8 bytes each
@res chars/rex2.bin
$684E AnimChar73 ; character 73, the restart marker: frames from FramesList3 $A77D (AnimateRestart $A740)
$6DD6 AnimChar250 ; characters 250-251: frames from FramesList2 $A789 (AnimateCells2 $A730)
$6DE6 AnimChar252 ; characters 252-255: AnimFramesA $AF82 / AnimFramesB $AFA2 on alternate passes (AnimateCells $A706)
$6E06 b CharAttrs 16 ; The attribute of each of the 256 room characters
@res chars/rex2.bin
$6F06 b BlockDefs 9 ; The 256 blocks: 3 x 3 character codes each, rows top to bottom
@res blocks/rex2.bin
$7806 b RoomMaps 10 ; The room maps: 7 rows of 10 block codes each (70 bytes a room); room n at $7806 + 70n; 35 slots, rooms 0-25 used
> The slots 26-34 ($8040-$8197, 630 bytes) are a leftover: no exit leads to them (RoomExits holds 26 rooms) and they are REX 1's rooms 26-34 with 44-69 of each room's 70 codes the same (work/stage2/NOTES.md); drawn with part 2's blocks they look like part 1's late rooms (tools/room_maps.py).
@res rooms/rex2-maps.bin
$8198 b Sprites 16 ; The sprites, pre-shifted: each label is a picture set its owner draws through a frame list
> $8198 is kind 0's picture (a walker, InitKind0 $CC05) and UpdateObject's default.
@res sprites/rex2.bin
$8258 SpriteHitFlash ; an object hit (HitObject, HitObjectHard)
$82B8 SpriteRamTurn ; the hit foot man turning (RamTurn $C032)
$8318 SpriteKind6 ; kind 6 and the hop (InitKind6 $CC18, StartHop $C5BE)
$8338 SpriteJumper ; a walker turned jumper (MakeJumper $C60D)
$8358 SpriteRex ; Rex walking (DrawRex)
$8418 SpriteRexJump ; Rex jumping or falling, off a lift (DrawRex)
$8490 SpriteRexDeath ; Rex's death; also the big squidgy thing's explosion pieces (BossExplodes $99E3)
$84D8 SpritePoints ; the points sign a kill leaves (KillObject $9807)
$8718 SpritePodA ; a pod left by an explosion (BlowUp)
$87D8 SpritePodB ; a pod left by an explosion (BlowUp)
$8898 SpritePowerPod ; the power pod's four frames ($8898, $88B8, $88D8, $88F8: AnimatePod $C1CB)
$8918 SpriteShield ; the shield bubble round Rex, 4 x 21 (DrawShield)
$8AC0 SpriteHudIcons ; the HUD's weapon and bomb icons
$8B60 SpriteHudIcons2 ; the HUD's weapon icons, second row
$8BA0 SpriteBonusPod ; the bonus pod (BlowUp)
$8BC0 SpriteBonusPod2 ; the bonus pod (BlowUp, InitBonusPod $CCBF)
$8BE0 SpriteKind3 ; kind 3 (InitKind3 $CC53)
$8D20 SpriteKind2 ; kind 2 (InitKind2 $CC75)
$8E20 SpriteKind5 ; kind 5 (InitKind5 $CCF3)
$8F00 SpriteKind1 ; kind 1 (InitKind1 $CC40)
$8FC0 SpriteKind4 ; kind 4 (InitKind4 $CC9D)
$9040 SpriteKind9 ; kind 9 (InitKind9 $CCD1)
$9100 SpriteKind14 ; kind 14, the mine (InitKind14 $CD15)
$9180 ExplosionPicture ; an exploding object's picture (UpdateObject $BC50); part 1 copied its own to $6018

